rising alarms about the dangers of the industry. Meanwhile, Trump has dismissed the warnings, and a divided US Congress has failed to act.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Criticism of LGBTQ+ raids in Turkey is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3257ce9b1b261044f449e725b0fee101cad0cc0e4e35a247bacc75c23f15360b</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/criticism-of-lgbtq-raids-in-turkey-is-growing/a-79284021--6d16d753143a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/criticism-of-lgbtq-raids-in-turkey-is-growing/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>High fuel prices challenge the German government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:232b31482b5802799128337c6cd5590f93bf05fb287f530cf5d902449e0dd837</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/high-fuel-prices-challenge-the-german-government/a-79282456--5be8e497a4c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/high-fuel-prices-challenge-the-german-government/a-79282456?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz wants to provide relief to motorists. But exactly how this is to happen remains unclear.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Knobloch: 'It is a very dangerous situation at the moment'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b40f4c1487aef5ef793ffe07071e4c56fc1c87f40c8f2bc905d5c00c1f86d85f</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/knobloch-it-is-a-very-dangerous-situation-at-the-moment/a-79278429--7a4fe86839bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/knobloch-it-is-a-very-dangerous-situation-at-the-moment/a-79278429?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Charlotte Knobloch survived the Holocaust by passing as the daughter of non-Jewish farmers. She recently spoke with DW to express her shock following the AfD victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa now probing deaths of 8 women near Johannesburg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e191ec1d16081daef37a43ca0ac3082142c1c377934c335493edb9b893ce487f</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-now-probing-deaths-of-8-women-near-johannesburg/a-79278296--101711badc97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-now-probing-deaths-of-8-women-near-johannesburg/a-79278296?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have warned women to take extra care in parts of Johannesburg as similarities between at least eight deaths fuel fears that the cases could be connected.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why do authoritarian regimes target the LGBTQ+ community?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:881d8dfdb45ecef3d7d48da80099bf3ce0cd3ae8fb8f470f1ed5e5ff93a85953</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831--8b4048f7a695.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A recent crackdown on the LGBTQ+ community in Turkey is symptomatic of a wider rights regression, according to experts. It's worse under authoritarian regimes, but why is it such a popular policy for these states?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Trump's Ukraine ceasefire proposal is 'good idea'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f11bdb4ff230b870907bb9698cbca40a01a9c37a367d731645c1b17a741f6e8f</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-trump-s-ukraine-ceasefire-proposal-is-good-idea/a-79280087--b477b9b94e84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-trump-s-ukraine-ceasefire-proposal-is-good-idea/a-79280087?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Kremlin has hailed an "energy ceasefire" proposed by US President Trump, but has criticized a French initiative to share its nuclear deterrent. Meanwhile, hostilities have continued on the ground and in the air.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ovechkin still backing Putin party in parliamentary vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a9806160ba5cd654339dc3e9014b7d0c454b5377341e699672d3e12fcd975d1</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ovechkin-still-backing-putin-party-in-parliamentary-vote/a-79277772--a3d39dd4a405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ovechkin-still-backing-putin-party-in-parliamentary-vote/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish scientists find first evidence of Diplodocus dinosaur in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:095c323f34670a53f297abc1b450889c32182dd89315b4c21ba8098922904784</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825--f2d2e7bb0613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paleontologists in Spain say they have found the first evidence of the long-necked Diplodocus genus of dinosaur outside of North America. They found bones at the rich La Tejeria fossil site in Teruel in eastern Spain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia faces hard choices as Houthis gain in Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f59ab4b68c0246ed2fbdfd994db175d63f3f61b362290e2e2b53df7e0e0053b</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-faces-hard-choices-as-houthis-gain-in-yemen/a-79274826--836e117689a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-faces-hard-choices-as-houthis-gain-in-yemen/a-79274826?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia faces growing security and economic problems as it seeks to balance deterrence and diplomacy during its escalating conflict with the Iran-backed Houthis in neighboring Yemen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09544efd2542bf73d6c82607cdabb066409ff95f02ff1f4ce8f66a37dcca2ad2</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the country's growing debt burden. And will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3ad7174fb4b2320b84652d9e57a7f5428bfc1cf43daa6f1b9472cf6d4d95cd7</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Woman, Life, Freedom' spirit lives on as Iran war drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f15c3d63f372f468f90fdec511fa7c1cdc2ed9089dd2395b9b8151495af339d</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-as-iran-war-drags-on/a-79276123--90098f2ae3f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-as-iran-war-drags-on/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2022 death of Jina Mahsa Amini in police custody triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bangladesh court sentences 7 Hasina allies to death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fc3bef5751f24fcf2e035ff5d975e175231db7319f2950642905495c6c5c92a</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bangladesh-court-sentences-7-hasina-allies-to-death/a-79276131--93bfc83fec03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bangladesh-court-sentences-7-hasina-allies-to-death/a-79276131?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest verdict brings to 22 the number of death sentences handed down in cases stemming from the 2024 uprising that ended Sheikh Hasina's 15-year rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Socialist Left leads far-right AfD ahead of Berlin vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33d6f526fba83934cd0e50dd67b63064b6f30f61e27ede7f2b18a80caecc8dcd</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/socialist-left-leads-far-right-afd-ahead-of-berlin-vote/a-79256516--23dd67cf573c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/socialist-left-leads-far-right-afd-ahead-of-berlin-vote/a-79256516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The results of the Berlin election are as hard to predict as ever. Three parties are vying for first place, including the socialist Left Party and the far-right AfD. But one issue is most important to Berliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz to cancel UN trip amid party infighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff81a66dc2c581968db2f62a1e7668e11b722fdcdcbbed481fe89e616c30d619</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-cancel-un-trip-over-party-infighting/live-79273324--971a6ac4ea62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-cancel-un-trip-amid-party-infighting/live-79273324?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's chancellor nixxed his trip over doubts about his leadership after party losses to the AfD in state elections. Meanwhile, Defense Minister Pistorius is in Washington for talks with his US counterpart.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SPD governor campaigns as one-woman bulwark against AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:462104044b459afba1119c68863744c482e0f005f81f3e29bac3b5762dd791b7</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225--0135376188de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuela Schwesig, of the center-left SPD, has governed the state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, on the Baltic Sea coast, since 2017. Ahead of this weekend's election, she is campaigning against the nationalist AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US confirms it has weapons in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efdc6464653a637283083f937c68e9f4f10503461b316f54ba58331fcceffb5b</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-confirms-it-has-weapons-in-space/a-79268894--7b3b13289f4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-confirms-it-has-weapons-in-space/a-79268894?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Space Force justified the weapons deployment by citing the US's two biggest geopolitical rivals: Russia and China. Beijing responded by urging Washington to "stop preparing for war" in outer space.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NATO jets shoot down drone over Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dfe393535300e2605e198453f450bbc03c104cd2e81d89ec0855a77fffc34bf</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nato-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania/a-79267975--4d3ef910416c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nato-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania/a-79267975?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The drone, which is believed to have entered Lithuanian airspace from Belarus, was shot down by an Italian fighter jet in between the cities of Vilnius and Kaunas. There have been no reports of casualties or damage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian warship fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b7c23ceac18c308699abe6b89f116e62d55a8c69463e8bb6a123ee49fbf55b0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-warship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter/a-79270510--158a6506bc4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-warship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter/a-79270510?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denmark has summoned Russia's ambassador over a Baltic Sea encounter that Copenhagen says is part of an increasingly aggressive pattern of Russian behavior.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
